    {
      "id": "p0154-b020",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "This prank call based on an English pun wouldn't work in Japanese, so the translator replaced it with a reference to Licca-chan, a classic Japanese toy doll famous for having a real-life telephone hotline. But instead of answering as Licca-chan, he asks if he's Licca-chan. And just like in the English scene, Sans isn't calling as a prank - he's asking a genuine question. Thus, through creative localization, Sans' English, pun-based anti-joke became a phone-themed anti joke with a cultural reference that Japanese players could recognize.",
        "raw": "This prank call based on an English pun wouldn't work in Japanese, so the\ntranslator replaced it with a reference to Licca-chan, a classic Japanese toy doll\nfamous for having a real-life telephone hotline. But instead of answering as\nLicca-chan, he asks if he's Licca-chan. And just like in the English scene, Sans\nisn't calling as a prank - he's asking a genuine question. Thus, through creative\nlocalization, Sans' English, pun-based anti-joke became a phone-themed anti\njoke with a cultural reference that Japanese players could recognize.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29810158,
          0.77312857,
          0.90208563,
          0.89465
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28872591,
          0.77241429,
          0.90748959,
          0.89572143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          49,
          50,
          51,
          52,
          53,
          54,
          55
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "这个基于英语双关的电话恶作剧，在日语中行不通，于是译者改为引用日本经典玩偶莉卡（Licca-chan），它以现实中的电话热线而闻名。但 Sans 并不是以莉卡的身份接电话，而是在问自己是不是莉卡。和英语版一样，他没有恶作剧，而是在认真提问。经过这样的创造性本地化，原本以英语双关构成的反笑话，变成了以电话为主题、包含日本玩家熟悉典故的反笑话。",
